From ec0edac06969e2ef98c0285f044be6735bfab69d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 02:27:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Load the gift shop from the database instead of a
 hardcoded list

The shop rendered 25 gifts hardcoded in this component, on their own
price scale (Rose 5, Diamond 100, Mansion 1000). The virtual_gifts table
was never read, so the 109-gift catalogue that now lives there - with
categories, prices, VIP tiers and artwork - was invisible to users.

This reads the catalogue at mount and renders it:

- 109 gifts across 11 categories, ordered by sort_order (category, then
  price ascending) rather than a hardcoded popularity number
- Category tabs are derived from the data, so adding a category is a
  database change and not a deploy
- Artwork comes from image_url (public SVG in Supabase Storage), with
  the emoji in `icon` as the per-card fallback if a file fails to load
- Postcards (is_wide) get a double-width tile so their wording stays
  readable
- Loading and error states, since the grid is now asynchronous

art_svg is deliberately excluded from the query. It holds the inline SVG
for every gift, about 639 kB across the table, and would ship on every
open of the shop; image_url points at the same artwork as a separately
cacheable file.

Sending is untouched: the same creditManager charge, the same staff-free
path, and the same delivery into the recipient's mail thread.

